      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 57-year-old woman presented with pain in her upper right abdomen, since 3 days. Laboratory tests showed elevated inflammation markers and an increased amount of alkaline phosphatase. Abdominal CT showed a perforating object from the stomach, ending in the liver. Gastroscopy revealed that the object was a fish bone."},
